## Source System Tables (Raw Layer)

### Table 1: pc_policyperiod
**Source System:** Guidewire PolicyCenter (Olos Release, December 2025)  
**Purpose:** Stores policy-level information including coverage decisions and HB 2067-relevant cancellation/declination/non-renewal reasons  
**Record Count:** ~5,000 (sample dataset); Production: 500,000+  
**Last Updated:** April 17, 2026  
**Refresh Frequency:** Real-time (via Informatica CDI streaming)  
**Storage Location:** BigQuery (`driiiportfolio.raw_underwriting_data.pc_policyperiod`)  
**Backup Strategy:** Daily snapshots retained for 90 days

#### Fields Documentation

---

##### PolicyNumber
Column Name: PolicyNumber Data Type: STRING(50) Length: 50 characters (max) Nullable: NO Primary Key: YES (part of composite with EffectiveDate) Foreign Key: Links to bc_policy.PolicyNumber Business Definition: Unique identifier assigned by PolicyCenter to each policy. Format: TFBC-[YYYY][SEQUENTIAL]. Example: TFBC-2026001234. Technical Description: Source: Guidewire sequence generator. Immutable after initial creation. Used as join key with BillingCenter and Location tables. Validation Rules: - Must match regex: ^TFBC-\d{4}\d{6}$ - Cannot be null or empty string - Must be unique (no duplicates allowed) Quality Rule ID: SOP-3.3 (Referential Integrity) Data Owner: Underwriting Operations Manager Sample Values: TFBC-2026001234, TFBC-2026005678, TFBC-2026009999 Known Issues: None reported (baseline accuracy 100%) HB 2067 Applicability: YES – Required for all statutory reports (TDI Section G) TDI Mapping: 28 TAC §5.9503 – Market Conduct Annual Statement (MCAS) Lineage: PolicyCenter → Informatica CDI → BigQuery Staging → Cleansed View

Code

---

##### Status
Column Name: Status Data Type: STRING(50) Length: 50 characters (max) Nullable: NO Primary Key: NO Foreign Key: NO Business Definition: Current lifecycle status of the policy. Indicates whether the policy is active, cancelled, declined, or in draft status. Technical Description: Controlled vocabulary from Guidewire PolicyCenter status list. Transitions managed by state machine in Olos release. Validation Rules: - Allowable values: 'Active', 'Canceled', 'Declined', 'Draft', 'NonRenewed', 'Suspended', 'Withdrawn' - Must not be null - Canceled/Declined/NonRenewed policies MUST have CancellationReasonCode populated Quality Rule ID: SOP-3.1 (Mandatory Fields) Data Owner: Underwriting Operations Manager Sample Values: 'Active', 'Canceled', 'NonRenewed' Known Issues: 140 canceled policies have NULL CancellationReasonCode (HB 2067 violation) HB 2067 Applicability: YES – Status drives reason code requirement TDI Mapping: 28 TAC §5.9503(g) – Actions reported: Cancellation (C), Non-renewal (NR), Declination (D) Lineage: PolicyCenter → Informatica CDI → BigQuery Staging → Cleansed View

Code

---

##### CancellationReasonCode
Column Name: CancellationReasonCode Data Type: STRING(10) Length: 10 characters (max) Nullable: YES (but conditionally mandatory if Status IN ('Canceled', 'NonRenewed', 'Declined')) Primary Key: NO Foreign Key: YES – References TDI_Reason_Mapping.InternalCode Business Definition: Internal business code explaining why a policy was canceled, declined, or not renewed. Must map to TDI statutory codes (A–X) per House Bill 2067. Technical Description: Populated by PolicyCenter automated underwriting system or manual entry by underwriters. Guidewire Olos release includes validation endpoint support for mapping validation. Validation Rules: - IF Status IN ('Canceled', 'NonRenewed', 'Declined') THEN CancellationReasonCode cannot be NULL - If provided, must exist in TDI_Reason_Mapping.InternalCode - When multiple reasons apply, codes are concatenated alphabetically (e.g., 'D|E|K' for Physical + Geographic + Roof condition) - Maximum 10 characters (accommodates multi-code concatenation) Quality Rule ID: SOP-3.1 (HB 2067 Compliance); SOP-3.5 (Value Constraints) Data Owner: Underwriting Manager Sample Values: 'D', 'E', 'K', 'D|E', 'B|D|K' Known Issues: 58 records have unmapped codes (internal system codes not in TDI reference table) 82 records missing code entirely despite Status = 'Canceled' HB 2067 Applicability: YES – CRITICAL – This is the primary field for HB 2067 compliance. Column 17 (Reason Codes) in TDI statistical report must match this field (concatenated alphabetically). TDI Mapping: 28 TAC §5.9503 Section E (Residential), Section F (Auto), Section G (Reconciliation) TDI Statutory Codes: A, B, C, D, E, F, G, H, I, J, K, L, M, N, O, P, Q, R, X Lineage: PolicyCenter → Informatica CDI → BigQuery Staging → TDI_Reason_Mapping lookup → vw_pc_policyperiod_cleansed (Cleansed_TDICode)

Code

---

##### CancellationDate
Column Name: CancellationDate Data Type: DATE Length: N/A (date format: YYYY-MM-DD) Nullable: YES (NULL if Status = 'Active' or 'Draft') Primary Key: NO Foreign Key: NO Business Definition: The effective date when the policy cancellation, declination, or non-renewal became effective. Used for HB 2067 retroactive data capture: notices sent before April 1, 2026 with effective date on or after April 1, 2026 must be included in June 15, 2026 report. Technical Description: Guidewire timestamp converted to DATE (time component discarded). Stored in UTC, converted to Central Time for reporting. Validation Rules: - If Status IN ('Canceled', 'NonRenewed', 'Declined'), CancellationDate cannot be NULL - Must be >= policy EffectiveDate - Must be <= CURRENT_DATE + 30 (reasonable future limit) - For HB 2067 reporting: If action effective date >= '2026-04-01', notice must be included even if sent before April 1, 2026 Quality Rule ID: SOP-3.2 (Logical Checks) Data Owner: Underwriting Operations Manager Sample Values: '2026-04-05', '2026-03-15', '2026-04-30' Known Issues: None (baseline accuracy 100%) HB 2067 Applicability: YES – Used for Phase 1 reporting cutoff and retroactive data capture logic TDI Mapping: 28 TAC §5.9503(g) – Retroactive capture: "if the action effective date falls on or after April 1, 2026" Lineage: PolicyCenter → Informatica CDI → BigQuery Staging → Cleansed View

Code

---

##### EffectiveDate
Column Name: EffectiveDate Data Type: DATE Length: N/A (date format: YYYY-MM-DD) Nullable: NO Primary Key: NO Foreign Key: NO Business Definition: The date when the policy becomes active or a coverage decision is effective. Used for temporal analysis and filtering by policy year. Technical Description: Set by PolicyCenter at binding. Immutable after policy creation. Validation Rules: - Cannot be NULL - Must be a valid calendar date - Must be <= CURRENT_DATE (no future-dated policies) - For renewals, EffectiveDate increments by policy term (typically 12 months) Quality Rule ID: SOP-3.2 (Logical Checks) Data Owner: Underwriting Operations Manager Sample Values: '2026-01-15', '2026-02-01', '2026-03-01' Known Issues: None reported HB 2067 Applicability: YES – Determines if policy falls within Q2 2026 reporting window TDI Mapping: 28 TAC §5.9503 – Statistical reports organized by effective date Lineage: PolicyCenter → Informatica CDI → BigQuery Staging → Cleansed View

Code

---

##### ExpirationDate
Column Name: ExpirationDate Data Type: DATE Length: N/A (date format: YYYY-MM-DD) Nullable: NO Primary Key: NO Foreign Key: NO Business Definition: The date when policy coverage terminates (typically 12 months after EffectiveDate). Used for determining active policy status and calculating pro-rata premium adjustments. Technical Description: Calculated by PolicyCenter as EffectiveDate + PolicyTerm. Standard term: 12 months. Renewable policies loop back to new EffectiveDate. Validation Rules: - Cannot be NULL - Must be > EffectiveDate - Typical range: 12 months after EffectiveDate Quality Rule ID: SOP-3.2 (Logical Checks) Data Owner: Underwriting Operations Manager Sample Values: '2027-01-15', '2027-02-01', '2027-03-01' Known Issues: None reported HB 2067 Applicability: NO (informational only for policy lifecycle tracking) TDI Mapping: N/A Lineage: PolicyCenter → Informatica CDI → BigQuery Staging → Cleansed View

Code

---

##### TotalPremium
Column Name: TotalPremium Data Type: DECIMAL(10,2) Length: Precision 10, Scale 2 (max $99,999,999.99) Nullable: NO Primary Key: NO Foreign Key: NO Business Definition: Total annual or policy-period premium amount charged to the insured. Used for financial reconciliation and rate adequacy testing. Technical Description: Calculated by PolicyCenter rating engine based on risk attributes, territory, coverage limits, and rating rules. Includes all surcharges and credits. Transmitted nightly to BillingCenter for invoice generation. Validation Rules: - Cannot be NULL - Must be > 0.00 (negative premiums not allowed) - Precision: 2 decimal places (cents) - Maximum: $99,999,999.99 (for excess insurance scenarios) Quality Rule ID: SOP-3.1 (Value Constraints) Data Owner: Actuarial Manager Sample Values: 1250.00, 3500.75, 15000.50 Known Issues: 204 records show discrepancy with BillingCenter (pro-rata calculation mismatch) HB 2067 Applicability: NO (not directly reported, but used for financial reconciliation) TDI Mapping: N/A Lineage: PolicyCenter → Informatica CDI → BigQuery Staging → vw_financial_reconciliation (for PC_Premium vs. BC_Premium comparison)

Code

---

##### AgentID
Column Name: AgentID Data Type: STRING(20) Length: 20 characters (max) Nullable: NO Primary Key: NO Foreign Key: YES – References Agent Master Table Business Definition: Unique identifier of the agent or agency that produced the policy. Used for agent performance analytics and agency relationship tracking. Technical Description: Integration with Microsoft Dynamics 365 for agency relationship data. Format: TFBC-AGENT-[000001] (6-digit sequential identifier). Validation Rules: - Cannot be NULL - Must exist in Agent Master reference table - Must be actively licensed per TDI records (validated via TDI master file quarterly) Quality Rule ID: SOP-3.3 (Referential Integrity) Data Owner: Agency Operations Manager Sample Values: 'TFBC-AGENT-001234', 'TFBC-AGENT-005678' Known Issues: None reported (referential integrity validated at binding) HB 2067 Applicability: NO (used for internal analytics, not statutory reporting) TDI Mapping: N/A (agent data tracked separately in TDI licensing records) Lineage: PolicyCenter → Informatica CDI → BigQuery Staging → Cleansed View

Code

---

##### IsMostRecentModel
Column Name: IsMostRecentModel Data Type: BOOLEAN (stored as 1/0) Length: N/A Nullable: NO Primary Key: NO Foreign Key: NO Business Definition: Flag indicating whether this record is the most current version of the policy period. Used to avoid counting the same policy multiple times when endorsements create new period records. Technical Description: Set to 1 (TRUE) when the record is created. Set to 0 (FALSE) when a new endorsement/amendment creates a replacement period record. Guarantees data uniqueness in aggregations. Validation Rules: - Cannot be NULL - Must be 1 (TRUE) or 0 (FALSE) - Exactly one record per PolicyNumber should have IsMostRecentModel = 1 - When IsMostRecentModel = 0, a corresponding record with value 1 must exist for the same PolicyNumber Quality Rule ID: SOP-3.3 (Referential Integrity) Data Owner: Data Quality Analyst II Sample Values: 1, 0 Known Issues: None (enforced by database constraint) HB 2067 Applicability: YES – Critical for accuracy: ensures canceled policies are counted only once in TDI reports TDI Mapping: 28 TAC §5.9503(g) – Section G Reconciliation: "Each unique policy action is counted once" Lineage: PolicyCenter → Informatica CDI → BigQuery Staging → Cleansed View

