##### County
Column Name: County Data Type: STRING(50) Length: 50 characters (max) Nullable: YES Primary Key: NO Foreign Key: NO Business Definition: County where the insured property is located (e.g., "Harris", "Galveston"). Used for catastrophe modeling and coastal risk identification. Technical Description: Extracted from address via geocoding service or manual entry. Validates against Texas county list (254 Texas counties). Validation Rules: - If provided, must be valid Texas county name - Coastal counties for catastrophe modeling: Harris, Galveston, Nueces, Cameron - Case-insensitive matching applied during validation Quality Rule ID: SOP-3.2 (Logical Checks) Data Owner: Underwriting Operations Manager Sample Values: 'Harris', 'Galveston', 'Travis', 'Dallas' Known Issues: 594 coastal county records missing Latitude/Longitude (geocoding gaps) HB 2067 Applicability: NO (used for risk assessment, not statutory reporting) TDI Mapping: N/A Lineage: PolicyCenter → Informatica CDI → BigQuery Staging → Cleansed View

