##### Latitude
Column Name: Latitude Data Type: FLOAT64 Length: Precision: decimal degrees (e.g., 29.760427) Nullable: YES (mandatory if County IN coastal risk counties) Primary Key: NO Foreign Key: NO Business Definition: Geographic latitude coordinate (North-South position) of the insured property. Used for catastrophe modeling and natural disaster risk assessment. Technical Description: Populated via third-party geocoding service (HazardHub API) or manual entry. Decimal degrees format (NAD83 datum). Range: 25.84 to 36.50 (Texas geographic bounds). Validation Rules: - If County IN ('Harris', 'Galveston', 'Nueces', 'Cameron'), Latitude cannot be NULL - Valid range: 25.84 to 36.50 (Texas bounds) - Precision: minimum 5 decimal places - If provided with Longitude, both must be present (no half-coordinates) Quality Rule ID: SOP-3.2 (Logical Checks), SOP-3.4 (Format Standards) Data Owner: Catastrophe Management Sample Values: 29.760427, 29.419220, 27.898363 Known Issues: 594 coastal county records have NULL Latitude Root cause: HazardHub API timeout failures HB 2067 Applicability: NO (used for underwriting risk assessment, not HB 2067 reporting) TDI Mapping: N/A Lineage: HazardHub API → Informatica CDI → BigQuery Staging → vw_pc_policylocation_cleansed (flagged as GEOCODE_REQUIRED if NULL)

