##### Longitude
Column Name: Longitude Data Type: FLOAT64 Length: Precision: decimal degrees (e.g., -95.369780) Nullable: YES (mandatory if County IN coastal risk counties) Primary Key: NO Foreign Key: NO Business Definition: Geographic longitude coordinate (East-West position) of the insured property. Used for catastrophe modeling and natural disaster risk assessment. Technical Description: Populated via HazardHub API or manual entry. Decimal degrees format (NAD83 datum). Range: -93.51 to -106.65 (Texas geographic bounds). Note: Western Hemisphere uses negative values. Validation Rules: - If County IN ('Harris', 'Galveston', 'Nueces', 'Cameron'), Longitude cannot be NULL - Valid range: -106.65 to -93.51 (Texas bounds) - Must be negative (Western Hemisphere) - Precision: minimum 5 decimal places - If provided with Latitude, both must be present Quality Rule ID: SOP-3.2 (Logical Checks), SOP-3.4 (Format Standards) Data Owner: Catastrophe Management Sample Values: -95.369780, -94.739092, -97.225110 Known Issues: 594 coastal county records have NULL Longitude Root cause: HazardHub API timeout failures HB 2067 Applicability: NO TDI Mapping: N/A Lineage: HazardHub API → Informatica CDI → BigQuery Staging → vw_pc_policylocation_cleansed (flagged as GEOCODE_REQUIRED if NULL)

