##### VIN
Column Name: VIN Data Type: STRING(17) Length: 17 characters (exactly) Nullable: YES (mandatory for auto policies, NULL acceptable for homeowner-only) Primary Key: NO Foreign Key: NO Business Definition: Vehicle Identification Number – unique identifier for automobiles. Used for rating, loss history lookup, and fraud detection. Format: 17-character alphanumeric per ISO 3779 standard. Technical Description: Entered by policyholder or sourced from vehicle registration. Used to query NHTSA (National Highway Traffic Safety Administration) database for vehicle specifications. Validation Rules: - For auto policies: Cannot be NULL - For homeowner policies: NULL acceptable (no vehicle) - Must be exactly 17 characters if provided - Must contain only alphanumeric characters (no spaces, hyphens, special chars) - Cannot contain digits 0, I, O, Q (prohibited by ISO standard) - First 3 characters (WMI): World Manufacturer Identifier (e.g., 1G1 = Chevrolet) - Position 10: Model year code (A=2010, B=2011, ..., H=2017, J=2018, K=2019, L=2020, M=2021, N=2022, P=2023, R=2024, T=2025, V=2026) Quality Rule ID: SOP-3.4 (Data Standards – Format Validation) Data Owner: Underwriting Manager Sample Values: '1HGBH41JXMN109186' (Honda Accord) '2G1FB1E39D1245678' (Chevrolet) '5TDJJRFH7LS123456' (Toyota Highlander) Known Issues: 344 records have malformed VINs: - 156 VINs with length != 17 - 188 VINs contain illegal characters (hyphens, spaces, etc.) - 0-value VINs indicating placeholder entry HB 2067 Applicability: NO (used for underwriting, not statutory reporting) TDI Mapping: N/A Lineage: PolicyCenter → Informatica CDI → BigQuery Staging → vw_pc_vehicle_cleansed (Sanitized_VIN field flags INVALID_FORMAT)

