## Reference Tables & Master Data

### Table 5: TDI_Reason_Mapping
**Source System:** Texas Department of Insurance (TDI) Statistical Plan 28 TAC §5.9503  
**Purpose:** Reference table mapping internal PolicyCenter reason codes to standardized TDI statutory codes (A–X). Critical for HB 2067 compliance verification.  
**Record Count:** 17 codes (A–X)  
**Last Updated:** April 17, 2026 (effective April 1, 2026)  
**Refresh Frequency:** Quarterly (whenever TDI updates statutory codes or new reason emerges)  
**Storage Location:** BigQuery (`driiiportfolio.raw_underwriting_data.TDI_Reason_Mapping`)  
**Backup Strategy:** Versioned; all historical versions retained for audit trail

#### Fields Documentation

---

##### InternalCode
Column Name: InternalCode Data Type: STRING(10) Length: 10 characters (max) Nullable: NO Primary Key: YES Foreign Key: N/A (reference key, not a true FK) Business Definition: Internal business code used within PolicyCenter to categorize cancellation/declination/non-renewal reasons. Examples: 'UnderwritingDeny', 'Fraud', 'NonPayment', etc. Technical Description: Free-text field allowing concatenation for multi-code scenarios (e.g., 'D|E|K' = Physical + Geographic + Roof). Validation Rules: - Cannot be NULL - Must be unique within the reference table - Used as JOIN key with pc_policyperiod.CancellationReasonCode Quality Rule ID: N/A (reference data) Data Owner: Underwriting Manager Sample Values: 'D', 'E', 'K', 'B', 'Fraud', 'NonPayment' Known Issues: 58 records in pc_policyperiod have CancellationReasonCode values not present in this reference table (unmapped codes) HB 2067 Applicability: YES – CRITICAL – This is the authoritative mapping for statutory compliance TDI Mapping: 28 TAC §5.9503 – TDI Statutory Reason Codes Lineage: TDI Statistical Plan → Manual entry into reference table → SQL validation join with pc_policyperiod

Code

---

##### TDICode
Column Name: TDICode Data Type: STRING(1) Length: 1 character (exactly) Nullable: NO Primary Key: NO Foreign Key: N/A (reference value) Business Definition: Standardized TDI reason code (A–X) as defined in Texas Statistical Plan 28 TAC §5.9503. This is the code reported to TDI in monthly/quarterly statistical reports. Technical Description: Single letter code representing one of 17 standardized reasons defined by TDI. When multiple reasons apply, codes are concatenated alphabetically in the report (e.g., 'DEK' for codes D, E, K combined). Validation Rules: - Cannot be NULL - Must be single character - Must be one of: A, B, C, D, E, F, G, H, I, J, K, L, M, N, O, P, Q, R, X Quality Rule ID: N/A (reference data) Data Owner: Compliance Officer Sample Values: 'A', 'B', 'D', 'K', 'X' Known Issues: None (static reference data, TDI-provided) HB 2067 Applicability: YES – CRITICAL – This exact code appears in Column 17 of TDI statistical reports TDI Mapping: 28 TAC §5.9503 – 17 authorized reason codes for residential and auto Lineage: TDI Statistical Plan → Reference table → pc_policyperiod Cleansed_TDICode → TDI Statistical Submission

Code

---

##### ReasonDescription
Column Name: ReasonDescription Data Type: STRING(100) Length: 100 characters (max) Nullable: NO Primary Key: NO Foreign Key: N/A Business Definition: Plain-English explanation of the TDI reason code. Used for training and documentation purposes. Technical Description: Descriptive text to help underwriting staff understand what each code represents. Validation Rules: - Cannot be NULL - Should not exceed 100 characters Quality Rule ID: N/A (reference data) Data Owner: Compliance Officer Sample Values: 'Aggressive or threatening behavior', 'Fraud or material misrepresentation', 'Failure to pay premium', 'Roof condition', 'Underwriting – All other reasons' Known Issues: None HB 2067 Applicability: NO (informational only) TDI Mapping: 28 TAC §5.9503 – Each code has official definition Lineage: TDI Statistical Plan → Reference table

Code

---

##### ApplicableTo
Column Name: ApplicableTo Data Type: STRING(50) Length: 50 characters (max) Nullable: NO Primary Key: NO Foreign Key: N/A Business Definition: Indicator of which action types this reason code is valid for: C (Cancellation), NR (Non-renewal), D (Declination). Not all codes apply to all actions. Technical Description: Concatenated flags: 'C', 'NR', 'D' combined as applicable (e.g., 'C, NR, D' = valid for all three actions). Validation Rules: - Cannot be NULL - Must contain subset of: C, NR, D - At least one action type must be specified Quality Rule ID: N/A (reference data; used in validation) Data Owner: Compliance Officer Sample Values: 'C, NR, D', 'NR', 'C', 'C, NR' Known Issues: None HB 2067 Applicability: YES – Used to validate that a code is appropriate for the policy action TDI Mapping: 28 TAC §5.9503 – Each code has defined applicability Lineage: TDI Statistical Plan → Reference table → Validation logic (ensures code C is used only for Cancellation actions, etc.)

