## Cleansed Views (Golden Layer)

The Golden Layer consists of four cleansed views that provide audit-compliant remediation while preserving the original raw data for audit trails.

### View 1: vw_pc_policyperiod_cleansed
**Purpose:** Remediated policy-period data with corrected HB 2067 reason codes for statutory reporting  
**Source Tables:** pc_policyperiod (base) + TDI_Reason_Mapping (lookup)  
**Creation Date:** April 18, 2026  
**Refresh Frequency:** Real-time (triggered on source table changes)  
**Storage Location:** BigQuery (`driiiportfolio.raw_underwriting_data.vw_pc_policyperiod_cleansed`)  
**Access Level:** Read-only

#### Remediation Logic

```sql
SELECT
    p.* EXCEPT(CancellationReasonCode),
    COALESCE(t.TDICode, 'K') as Cleansed_TDICode,  -- Default to 'K' (Underwriting) if unmapped
    CASE
        WHEN t.TDICode IS NULL AND Status = 'Canceled' THEN 'REMEDIATED'
        ELSE 'ORIGINAL'
    END as Remediation_Status
FROM pc_policyperiod p
LEFT JOIN TDI_Reason_Mapping t ON p.CancellationReasonCode = t.InternalCode
Added Fields
Cleansed_TDICode
Code
Column Name:              Cleansed_TDICode
Data Type:                STRING(1)
Length:                   1 character
Nullable:                 NO
Business Definition:      Remediated TDI reason code suitable for statutory reporting.
                         If original CancellationReasonCode had no TDI mapping, defaults to 'K' 
                         (Underwriting – All Other Underwriting Reasons) as legally permissible default.
Technical Description:    COALESCE(t.TDICode, 'K') – ensures every canceled policy has a valid 
                         TDI code for reporting.
Validation Rules:         - Always one of: A–X (never NULL)
                         - If Remediation_Status = 'REMEDIATED', code is 'K'
                         - If Remediation_Status = 'ORIGINAL', code matches TDI reference table
Quality Rule ID:          SOP-3.1 (HB 2067 Compliance)
Remediation Rule:         Default unmapped codes to 'K' per business rule approved by Underwriting Manager
Compliance Impact:        Enables TDI reporting of 100% of canceled policies (no NULL codes)
Sample Values:            'A', 'B', 'D', 'K'
Known Issues:            58 policies remediated with default code 'K' (original codes unmapped)
Audit Trail:              Original CancellationReasonCode preserved in p.CancellationReasonCode 
                         for audit purposes
HB 2067 Status:           ✓ COMPLIANT – All canceled policies have valid TDI codes
TDI Mapping:              28 TAC §5.9503 – Column 17 of statistical report
Remediation_Status
Code
Column Name:              Remediation_Status
Data Type:                STRING(20)
Length:                   20 characters (max)
Nullable:                 NO
Business Definition:      Flag indicating whether this record's TDI code is original (from 
                         source) or remediated (defaulted by system). Used for audit trail 
                         and tracking remediation effectiveness.
Technical Description:    CASE statement:
                         - 'ORIGINAL' = record had valid TDI code mapping in source
                         - 'REMEDIATED' = record had unmapped code, defaulted to 'K'
                         - 'ORIGINAL' for non-canceled policies (no remedi ation applicable)
Validation Rules:         - Must be 'ORIGINAL' or 'REMEDIATED'
                         - If Status != 'Canceled', Remediation_Status must be 'ORIGINAL'
                         - If Status = 'Canceled' and Cleansed_TDICode = 'K', 
                           Remediation_Status should be 'REMEDIATED' (unless original code was also 'K')
Quality Rule ID:          N/A (audit flag)
Audit Purpose:            Enables compliance auditors to identify which records received system-applied defaults
Sample Values:            'ORIGINAL', 'REMEDIATED'
Known Issues:            58 records with Remediation_Status = 'REMEDIATED' 
                         (original CancellationReasonCode was unmapped)
Audit Impact:             Records marked 'REMEDIATED' require sign-off from Data Governance Committee 
                         before Q2 TDI report submission
TDI Mapping:              N/A (internal audit field, not reported to TDI)
View 2: vw_pc_policylocation_cleansed
Purpose: Location data with geocoding health status flags for catastrophe modeling oversight
Source Tables: pc_policylocation (base) + pc_policyperiod (referential join)
Creation Date: April 18, 2026
Refresh Frequency: Real-time
Storage Location: BigQuery (driiiportfolio.raw_underwriting_data.vw_pc_policylocation_cleansed)
Access Level: Read-only

Remediation Logic
SQL
SELECT
    l.*,
    CASE
        WHEN Latitude IS NULL OR Longitude IS NULL THEN 'GEOCODE_REQUIRED'
        ELSE 'GEOCODE_VALID'
    END as Geo_Health_Status
FROM pc_policylocation l
INNER JOIN pc_policyperiod p ON l.BranchID = p.ID  -- Inner join removes orphans
Added Fields
Geo_Health_Status
Code
Column Name:              Geo_Health_Status
Data Type:                STRING(20)
Length:                   20 characters (max)
Nullable:                 NO
Business Definition:      Quality flag indicating whether a location has valid geocoding 
                         coordinates for catastrophe modeling. Used to identify locations 
                         requiring manual geocoding correction or vendor investigation.
Technical Description:    CASE statement evaluating Latitude and Longitude:
                         - 'GEOCODE_VALID' = both Latitude and Longitude are populated (not NULL)
                         - 'GEOCODE_REQUIRED' = either Latitude or Longitude is NULL
                         Applied to all locations; particularly critical for coastal counties 
                         (Harris, Galveston, Nueces, Cameron) where high-value properties 
                         require accurate CAT modeling.
Validation Rules:         - Must be 'GEOCODE_VALID' or 'GEOCODE_REQUIRED'
                         - If County IN ('Harris', 'Galveston', 'Nueces', 'Cameron'), 
                           Geo_Health_Status should be 'GEOCODE_VALID' (flagged if not)
Quality Rule ID:          SOP-3.2 (Logical Checks), validated via SQL_04_Geocoding_Completeness_Check
Remediation Rule:         Not auto-remediated; flagged for Catastrophe Management review 
                         and HazardHub API requery
Sample Values:            'GEOCODE_VALID', 'GEOCODE_REQUIRED'
Known Issues:            594 coastal county locations flagged as 'GEOCODE_REQUIRED'
                         Root cause: HazardHub API regional timeout (March 2026 incident)
Remediation Action:       Escalated to IT; HazardHub API infrastructure fix required; 
                         recommend reprocessing after API stability confirmed
HB 2067 Status:           N/A (not directly reported, used for underwriting oversight)
TDI Mapping:              N/A
Audit Trail:              Original NULL values preserved; flag only indicates status
View 3: vw_pc_vehicle_cleansed
Purpose: Vehicle data with VIN format validation flags for data quality control
Source Table: pc_vehicle
Creation Date: April 18, 2026
Refresh Frequency: Real-time
Storage Location: BigQuery (driiiportfolio.raw_underwriting_data.vw_pc_vehicle_cleansed)
Access Level: Read-only

Remediation Logic
SQL
SELECT
    PolicyNumber,
    VIN as Original_VIN,
    CASE
        WHEN LENGTH(VIN) = 17 AND NOT REGEXP_CONTAINS(VIN, r'[^a-zA-Z0-9]') 
            THEN VIN
        ELSE 'INVALID_FORMAT'
    END as Sanitized_VIN
FROM pc_vehicle
Added Fields
Original_VIN
Code
Column Name:              Original_VIN
Data Type:                STRING(17)
Length:                   17 characters (max)
Nullable:                 YES
Business Definition:      Raw VIN as entered in PolicyCenter, preserved for audit trail.
Technical Description:    Direct copy of source pc_vehicle.VIN field.
Validation Rules:         - Preserved as-is from source (no modification)
                         - Used for audit trail and change tracking
Quality Rule ID:          N/A (audit field)
Sample Values:            '1HGBH41JXMN109186', '1-G-G-B-H-4-1-J-X-M-N-1-0-9-1-8-6', 'INVALID'
Known Issues:            344 records with malformed VINs preserved as-is for investigation
HB 2067 Status:           N/A
TDI Mapping:              N/A
Sanitized_VIN
Code
Column Name:              Sanitized_VIN
Data Type:                STRING(17)
Length:                   17 characters (max)
Nullable:                 NO
Business Definition:      Standardized VIN after format validation. If original VIN passes 
                         ISO 3779 standard (17 alphanumeric characters, no special chars), 
                         Sanitized_VIN = Original_VIN. Otherwise, marked 'INVALID_FORMAT' 
                         for source system correction.
Technical Description:    CASE validation:
                         - IF LENGTH(VIN) = 17 AND NOT REGEXP_CONTAINS(VIN, r'[^a-zA-Z0-9]')
                         - THEN Sanitized_VIN = VIN
                         - ELSE Sanitized_VIN = 'INVALID_FORMAT'
                         Does NOT auto-correct; only identifies problematic records.
Validation Rules:         - Must be either 17-character valid VIN or 'INVALID_FORMAT'
                         - If 'INVALID_FORMAT', source system entry must be corrected manually
Quality Rule ID:          SOP-3.4 (Data Standards – Format Validation)
Remediation Rule:         Flagged for source system correction; not auto-remediated
Sample Values:            '1HGBH41JXMN109186' (valid), 'INVALID_FORMAT' (failed validation)
Known Issues:            344 records marked 'INVALID_FORMAT':
                         - 156 with incorrect length (not 17 chars)
                         - 188 containing hyphens, spaces, or other special characters
Remediation Action:       Underwriting staff must review original registration documents 
                         and re-enter in PolicyCenter; recommend batch ETL correction process
HB 2067 Status:           N/A
TDI Mapping:              N/A
View 4: vw_financial_reconciliation
Purpose: Cross-system premium reconciliation for financial integrity verification between PolicyCenter and BillingCenter
Source Tables: pc_policyperiod (PolicyCenter) + bc_policy (BillingCenter)
Creation Date: April 18, 2026
Refresh Frequency: Nightly (after BillingCenter load completes)
Storage Location: BigQuery (driiiportfolio.raw_underwriting_data.vw_financial_reconciliation)
Access Level: Read-only

Reconciliation Logic
SQL
SELECT
    pc.PolicyNumber,
    pc.TotalPremium as PC_Premium,
    bc.TotalPremium as BC_Premium,
    ROUND(bc.TotalPremium - pc.TotalPremium, 2) as Adjustment_Amount,
    CASE
        WHEN ABS(pc.TotalPremium - bc.TotalPremium) > 0.01 THEN 'DISCREPANCY'
        ELSE 'ALIGNED'
    END as Alignment_Status
FROM pc_policyperiod pc
JOIN bc_policy bc ON pc.PolicyNumber = bc.PolicyNumber
Added Fields
PC_Premium
Code
Column Name:              PC_Premium
Data Type:                DECIMAL(10,2)
Length:                   Precision 10, Scale 2
Nullable:                 NO
Business Definition:      Total premium from PolicyCenter (underwriting system of record).
Technical Description:    Copied directly from pc_policyperiod.TotalPremium.
Validation Rules:         - Must be > 0.00
Quality Rule ID:          N/A (source field)
Sample Values:            1250.00, 3500.75
HB 2067 Status:           N/A
TDI Mapping:              N/A
BC_Premium
Code
Column Name:              BC_Premium
Data Type:                DECIMAL(10,2)
Length:                   Precision 10, Scale 2
Nullable:                 NO
Business Definition:      Total premium from BillingCenter (billing system of record).
                         BillingCenter applies pro-rata calculations for daily changes.
Technical Description:    Copied directly from bc_policy.TotalPremium.
Validation Rules:         - Must be > 0.00
Quality Rule ID:          N/A (source field)
Sample Values:            1250.00, 3500.75
HB 2067 Status:           N/A
TDI Mapping:              N/A
Adjustment_Amount
Code
Column Name:              Adjustment_Amount
Data Type:                DECIMAL(10,2)
Length:                   Precision 10, Scale 2
Nullable:                 NO
Business Definition:      Dollar amount difference between BillingCenter and PolicyCenter 
                         premiums. Positive value = BillingCenter premium is higher; 
                         negative value = PolicyCenter premium is higher.
                         Used to identify pro-rata calculation errors.
Technical Description:    Calculated as: ROUND(bc.TotalPremium - pc.TotalPremium, 2)
                         Rounded to nearest cent for reporting and reconciliation.
Validation Rules:         - Rounded to exactly 2 decimal places
                         - Positive, negative, or zero values acceptable
                         - If ABS(Adjustment_Amount) > 100.00, escalate to Accounting review
Quality Rule ID:          SOP-3.5 (Cross-System Reconciliation)
Sample Values:            0.00 (no variance), 50.25 (BC higher), -75.10 (PC higher)
Known Issues:            204 policies with ABS(Adjustment_Amount) > 0.01:
                         - Average variance: $50–$200 per policy
                         - Total financial impact: ~$25,000 net discrepancy
                         - Root cause: BillingCenter pro-rata logic error
Remediation Action:       Accounting team investigating pro-rata calculation formula; 
                         software patch planned for April 2026 maintenance window
Audit Purpose:            Enables financial statement reconciliation; material variances 
                         tracked in General Ledger
HB 2067 Status:           N/A
TDI Mapping:              N/A
Alignment_Status
Code
Column Name:              Alignment_Status
Data Type:                STRING(20)
Length:                   20 characters (max)
Nullable:                 NO
Business Definition:      Flag indicating whether premiums align between systems within 
                         acceptable tolerance ($0.01 variance threshold).
Technical Description:    CASE statement:
                         - 'ALIGNED' = ABS(pc.TotalPremium - bc.TotalPremium) <= 0.01
                         - 'DISCREPANCY' = ABS(pc.TotalPremium - bc.TotalPremium) > 0.01
Validation Rules:         - Must be 'ALIGNED' or 'DISCREPANCY'
                         - Tolerance threshold: $0.01 (cent level)
Quality Rule ID:          SOP-3.5 (Cross-System Reconciliation)
Sample Values:            'ALIGNED', 'DISCREPANCY'
Known Issues:            204 records with Alignment_Status = 'DISCREPANCY'
Audit Process:            Finance team reviews DISCREPANCY records monthly; corrections 
                         made in GL reconciliation module
HB 2067 Status:           N/A
TDI Mapping:              N/A
