Glossary of Terms
Term	Definition
BranchID	Internal Guidewire database ID linking locations to policies (referential integrity key)
Cancellation Reason Code	Internal business code explaining policy cancellation/declination/non-renewal
CAT Modeling	Catastrophe modeling; assessment of natural disaster risk (earthquakes, hurricanes, etc.)
Cleansed Layer	Golden layer views providing remediated, audit-compliant data without modifying raw sources
Compliance Status	Validation result: 'Valid', 'Mapping Discrepancy', or 'Missing Mapping'
Data Dictionary	Comprehensive metadata registry defining all fields, types, constraints, and business meaning
Data Governance	Framework of policies, procedures, and controls ensuring data quality and compliance
Data Lineage	Trace of data origin, transformations, and destination through system layers
ETL	Extract-Transform-Load; process of moving data from source to target systems
Field	Individual column within a table (e.g., PolicyNumber, CancellationReasonCode)
Foreign Key	Reference to a primary key in another table; enables relational integrity
Geocoding	Process of converting address to latitude/longitude coordinates
Golden Layer	Cleansed, validated data suitable for reporting and compliance; preserves audit trail
HB 2067	House Bill 2067 (89th Texas Legislature, 2025); mandates automatic written denial explanations
INNER JOIN	SQL join retaining only rows with matches in both tables; removes orphans
Informatica IDMC	Cloud data integration platform; enables real-time data streaming and profiling
IPU	Informatica Pricing Unit; consumption-based billing model for IDMC services
ISO 3779	International standard defining VIN structure (17-character alphanumeric format)
LEFT JOIN	SQL join retaining all rows from left table; fills nulls from right table
Materialized View	Pre-computed, persistently stored query result (vs. virtual view computed on-demand)
Metadata	Data describing data (e.g., field names, types, definitions); enables governance
NHTSA	National Highway Traffic Safety Administration; authoritative VIN database
NULL	Absence of value; indicates missing, unknown, or not-applicable data
Orphan Records	Records lacking valid parent reference; violates referential integrity constraint
Primary Key	Unique identifier for each record within a table
Profiling	Statistical analysis of data quality (null counts, distinct values, outliers, etc.)
RCA	Root Cause Analysis; systematic investigation to identify systemic data quality failures
Referential Integrity	Database constraint requiring foreign keys to match existing primary keys
Regex	Regular expression; pattern-matching syntax for format validation
Remediation	Process of correcting data quality issues or implementing preventive measures
SLA	Service Level Agreement; response time commitments for issue resolution
Staging Layer	Temporary repository for raw data before profiling/transformation
TDI	Texas Department of Insurance; regulatory body overseeing insurance markets
UNION	SQL operation combining results from multiple queries into single result set
Validation Rule	Defined constraint (format, domain, business logic) that data must satisfy
View	Virtual table presenting filtered/transformed data from underlying base tables
WMI	World Manufacturer Identifier; first 3 VIN characters identifying vehicle manufacturer
