## Master Rule Registry

### VR-001-001: Cancellation Reason Code (Mandatory if Status = Canceled)

Rule ID: VR-001-001 Rule Name: HB 2067 Mandatory Cancellation Reason Category: Mandatory Fields Priority Level: CRITICAL SOP Reference: SOP 3.1 (Mandatory Fields) Description: Ensures all canceled policies have reason code populated. This is the PRIMARY HB 2067 compliance check; statutes require written explanation for every coverage denial.

SOURCE TABLE(S):

pc_policyperiod (primary)
TDI_Reason_Mapping (reference validation)
TARGET RECORD(S):

Policies with Status = 'Canceled'
Estimated volume (sample): 142 records out of 5,000 (2.84%)
Production volume: ~50,000 canceled policies annually
BUSINESS RULE: If Status IN ('Canceled', 'NonRenewed', 'Declined'): Then CancellationReasonCode MUST NOT be NULL And CancellationReasonCode MUST exist in TDI_Reason_Mapping.InternalCode

Regulatory Citation:

House Bill 2067, 89th Texas Legislature (2025)
Effective: April 1, 2026
Requirement: Automatic written explanation for coverage denial
28 TAC §5.9503 (Texas Insurance Code § [number])
TECHNICAL IMPLEMENTATION: Pseudo-SQL Logic:

CASE 1: Missing Reason Code IF Status = 'Canceled' AND CancellationReasonCode IS NULL THEN VIOLATION = TRUE

CASE 2: Unmapped Reason Code IF Status = 'Canceled' AND CancellationReasonCode NOT IN (SELECT InternalCode FROM TDI_Reason_Mapping) THEN VIOLATION = TRUE

ELSE: VALID

VALIDATION QUERY:

-- Detection Query: VR-001-001 SELECT 'VR-001-001' as Rule_ID, 'HB 2067 Mandatory Cancellation Reason' as Rule_Name, p.PolicyNumber, p.Status, p.CancellationReasonCode, t.TDICode, CASE WHEN p.Status = 'Canceled' AND p.CancellationReasonCode IS NULL THEN 'Missing Reason Code' WHEN p.Status = 'Canceled' AND p.CancellationReasonCode IS NOT NULL AND t.TDICode IS NULL THEN 'Unmapped Reason Code' ELSE 'VALID' END as Violation_Type, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP() as Detection_Time FROM driiiportfolio.raw_underwriting_data.pc_policyperiod p LEFT JOIN driiiportfolio.raw_underwriting_data.TDI_Reason_Mapping t ON p.CancellationReasonCode = t.InternalCode WHERE p.Status IN ('Canceled', 'NonRenewed', 'Declined') AND ( p.CancellationReasonCode IS NULL OR t.TDICode IS NULL ) ORDER BY p.PolicyNumber;

ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA:

Threshold: 0% (no canceled policies without reason codes)
Pass Condition: COUNT(violations) = 0
Current Status (April 2026): FAILING
Missing Codes: 82 records
Unmapped Codes: 58 records
Total Violations: 140 records
Violation Rate: 2.8% (EXCEEDS 0% threshold by 2.8%)
EXCEPTION HANDLING:

Auto-renewal policies: May default to 'NR' (Non-renewal) if renewal declined by system
Draft policies: Exempt (not yet active; reason not applicable)
Withdrawn policies: Treated same as Canceled (require reason code)
Approved Exceptions: None currently approved; all violations require remediation
SEVERITY CLASSIFICATION:

Data Quality Dimensions: Accuracy, Completeness, Validity
Business Impact: CRITICAL
Prevents HB 2067 statutory compliance reporting
Exposes organization to regulatory penalties
Violates TDI reporting requirements
Regulatory Exposure: HIGH (HB 2067 enforcement; TDI market conduct examination)
Customer Service Impact: Customers lack written denial explanation (violates law)
DETECTION TIMESTAMP:

Execution: Real-time (via Informatica CDI on policy status change)
Batch Verification: Nightly (SQL Server Agent job at 11:00 PM)
Latency Tolerance: <= 4 hours
Retry Logic: 2 retries on timeout (escalate to Informatica support if persistent)
REMEDIATION PATH:

Responsibility: Underwriting Operations Manager + Data Quality Analyst II
Remediation Method:
If Missing: Assign reason based on case notes / underwriter decision
If Unmapped: Map internal code to TDI code via TDI_Reason_Mapping table update
Expected Resolution Time: 24 hours
Preventive Measure: Guidewire Olos validation endpoint enforces at policy binding
HB 2067 APPLICABILITY:

YES (CRITICAL)
TDI Statutory Requirement: 28 TAC §5.9503(E, F, G)
Column Mapping: Column 17 (Reason Codes) in TDI statistical report
Report Due Date: June 15, 2026 (Phase 1 residential/auto)
Retroactive Capture: Notices sent before 4/1/2026 with action effective on/after 4/1/2026 must be included
PERFORMANCE METRICS:

Query Execution Time: 2.3 seconds (5,000 record sample)
Violations Detected: 140 records (2.8% of canceled policies)
False Positive Rate: 0% (rule is deterministic)
Maintenance Notes:
Performance: GOOD (indexed lookup on PolicyNumber)
Update Frequency: Real-time (critical for compliance)
Known Issues: Olos release missing cancellation trigger mappings (82 records)
Code

