### VR-001-002: Mandatory Agent ID

Rule ID: VR-001-002 Rule Name: Mandatory Agent ID for Policy Accountability Category: Mandatory Fields Priority Level: HIGH SOP Reference: SOP 3.1 Description: Ensures every policy has associated agent for accountability and commission tracking.

SOURCE TABLE(S):

pc_policyperiod (primary)
Agent Master (reference validation)
TARGET RECORD(S):

All policies
Estimated volume (sample): 5,000 records
Production: 500,000+ policies
BUSINESS RULE: For all policy records: AgentID MUST NOT be NULL AgentID MUST exist in Agent Master table Agent MUST have current Texas insurance license

TECHNICAL IMPLEMENTATION: IF AgentID IS NULL OR AgentID NOT IN (SELECT AgentID FROM Agent_Master WHERE LicenseStatus = 'Active') THEN VIOLATION = TRUE

VALIDATION QUERY:

SELECT 'VR-001-002' as Rule_ID, PolicyNumber, AgentID, 'Missing or Unlicensed Agent' as Violation_Type FROM driiiportfolio.raw_underwriting_data.pc_policyperiod p LEFT JOIN Agent_Master a ON p.AgentID = a.AgentID WHERE p.AgentID IS NULL OR a.AgentID IS NULL OR a.LicenseStatus != 'Active';

ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA:

Threshold: 0% (all policies must have active agent)
Pass Condition: COUNT(violations) = 0
Current Status: PASSING (0 violations detected)
EXCEPTION HANDLING:

Wholesale policies from other insurers: Exempt (handled via agency relationship)
Direct online policies: May have AgentID = 'DIRECT' (special placeholder)
SEVERITY CLASSIFICATION:

Business Impact: HIGH (affects commission processing and agent accountability)
Regulatory Exposure: MEDIUM (TDI agent tracking requirements)
DETECTION TIMESTAMP:

Execution: Nightly batch (11:00 PM)
Latency Tolerance: <= 4 hours
REMEDIATION PATH:

Responsibility: Underwriting Operations Manager
Method: Assign correct agent or mark as DIRECT online sale
Resolution Time: 24 hours
HB 2067 APPLICABILITY:

NO (operational; not directly reported to TDI)
PERFORMANCE METRICS:

