### VR-002-001: Premium > 0 (Value Constraint)

Rule ID: VR-002-001 Rule Name: Premium Amount Positivity Check Category: Value Constraints Priority Level: CRITICAL SOP Reference: SOP 3.1 Description: Ensures all policy premiums are positive (non-zero, non-negative). Negative or zero premiums indicate data entry errors or system issues.

SOURCE TABLE(S):

pc_policyperiod
TARGET RECORD(S):

All policies with Status = 'Active'
Estimated volume (sample): 4,200 active records (84% of 5,000)
BUSINESS RULE: For all active policies: TotalPremium MUST be > 0.00 Premium MUST be <= $99,999,999.99 (system maximum)

TECHNICAL IMPLEMENTATION: IF TotalPremium <= 0.00 OR TotalPremium > 99999999.99 THEN VIOLATION = TRUE

VALIDATION QUERY:

SELECT 'VR-002-001' as Rule_ID, PolicyNumber, Status, TotalPremium, CASE WHEN TotalPremium <= 0.00 THEN 'Non-Positive Premium' WHEN TotalPremium > 99999999.99 THEN 'Exceeds Maximum' ELSE 'VALID' END as Violation_Type FROM driiiportfolio.raw_underwriting_data.pc_policyperiod WHERE Status = 'Active' AND (TotalPremium <= 0.00 OR TotalPremium > 99999999.99);

ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA:

Threshold: 0% (all active policies must have positive premium)
Pass Condition: COUNT(violations) = 0
Current Status: PASSING (0 violations)
EXCEPTION HANDLING:

Zero-premium promotional policies: Require explicit override approval
Binder period: May allow zero premium temporarily; must update at binding
SEVERITY CLASSIFICATION:

Data Quality Dimensions: Accuracy, Validity
Business Impact: CRITICAL (prevents financial reporting and billing)
Regulatory Exposure: HIGH (impacts financial statements and loss ratios)
DETECTION TIMESTAMP:

Execution: Real-time (at policy binding in PolicyCenter)
Latency Tolerance: Immediate
REMEDIATION PATH:

