### VR-002-002: Effective Date < Expiration Date (Logical Check)

Rule ID: VR-002-002 Rule Name: Policy Term Date Logic (Start < End) Category: Logical Checks Priority Level: CRITICAL SOP Reference: SOP 3.2 Description: Validates policy effective date precedes expiration date. Reverse or equal dates indicate data entry errors.

SOURCE TABLE(S):

pc_policyperiod
TARGET RECORD(S):

All policies (Active, Canceled, Draft)
Estimated volume (sample): 5,000 records
BUSINESS RULE: For all policies: EffectiveDate < ExpirationDate Typical policy term: 12 months (can vary for multi-year contracts)

TECHNICAL IMPLEMENTATION: IF EffectiveDate >= ExpirationDate THEN VIOLATION = TRUE

VALIDATION QUERY:

SELECT 'VR-002-002' as Rule_ID, PolicyNumber, EffectiveDate, ExpirationDate, TIMESTAMP_DIFF(ExpirationDate, EffectiveDate, DAY) as Term_Days, 'Date Logic Violation' as Violation_Type FROM driiiportfolio.raw_underwriting_data.pc_policyperiod WHERE EffectiveDate >= ExpirationDate;

