### VR-003-001: VIN Format Validation

Rule ID: VR-003-001 Rule Name: Vehicle Identification Number (VIN) Format Validation Category: Format Standards Priority Level: MEDIUM SOP Reference: SOP 3.4 Description: Validates VIN format per ISO 3779 standard (17-character alphanumeric). Enables NHTSA vehicle specification lookups and rating accuracy.

SOURCE TABLE(S):

pc_vehicle
TARGET RECORD(S):

Auto policies with vehicles
Estimated volume (sample): 3,800 records
Estimated violations: 344 records (9.05%)
BUSINESS RULE: For all vehicle records (auto policies): VIN MUST NOT be NULL VIN MUST be exactly 17 characters VIN MUST contain only alphanumeric characters (no hyphens, spaces, or special chars) VIN MUST NOT contain prohibited digits: 0, I, O, Q (per ISO 3779) Position 10 (model year code) MUST be valid: A–Y (excluding I, O, Q, U, Z)

TECHNICAL IMPLEMENTATION: IF LENGTH(VIN) != 17 OR REGEXP_CONTAINS(VIN, r'[^a-zA-Z0-9]') -- Contains non-alphanumeric OR REGEXP_CONTAINS(VIN, r'[0IOQ]') -- Contains prohibited chars THEN VIOLATION = TRUE

VALIDATION QUERY:

SELECT 'VR-003-001' as Rule_ID, PolicyNumber, VIN as Original_VIN, LENGTH(VIN) as VIN_Length, CASE WHEN VIN IS NULL THEN 'Missing VIN' WHEN LENGTH(VIN) != 17 THEN 'Invalid Length: ' || LENGTH(VIN) WHEN REGEXP_CONTAINS(VIN, r'[^a-zA-Z0-9]') THEN 'Contains Special Characters' WHEN REGEXP_CONTAINS(VIN, r'[0IOQ]') THEN 'Contains Prohibited Characters' ELSE 'VALID' END as Violation_Type, 'Format Standards' as Category FROM driiiportfolio.raw_underwriting_data.pc_vehicle WHERE LENGTH(VIN) != 17 OR REGEXP_CONTAINS(VIN, r'[^a-zA-Z0-9]') OR REGEXP_CONTAINS(VIN, r'[0IOQ]');

ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA:

Threshold: < 5% (historical data may have legacy formats)
Pass Condition: Violation_Rate < 5%
Current Status: FAILING
Invalid Length: 156 records
Special Characters: 188 records
Total Violations: 344 records
Violation Rate: 9.05% (EXCEEDS 5% threshold by 4.05%)
EXCEPTION HANDLING:

Bikes/motorcycles: May have shorter VINs (12–17 chars); document as exception
Non-U.S. vehicles: May use different standards; require documentation
Legacy/classic vehicles: May lack factory VIN; use placeholder 'UNKNOWN_VIN_CLASSIC'
SEVERITY CLASSIFICATION:

Impact: MEDIUM (prevents rating accuracy; complicates loss history lookup)
Business Impact: Cannot validate vehicle specifications; may under/over-rate
Regulatory Exposure: LOW (not directly HB 2067-related)
DETECTION TIMESTAMP:

Execution: Nightly batch (11:00 PM)
Latency Tolerance: <= 4 hours
REMEDIATION PATH:

Responsibility: Underwriting team (data entry correction)
Method: Re-enter VIN from registration document
Resolution Time: 5 business days
Preventive: Guidewire validation at policy binding
HB 2067 APPLICABILITY:

NO
PERFORMANCE METRICS:

Query Execution Time: 1.9 seconds
Violations Detected: 344 records (9.05%)
False Positive Rate: 0%
Maintenance Notes:
Known Issue: Legacy system data migration without normalization
Recommendation: Batch cleansing process for historical records
