### VR-004-002: Cross-System Policy Reconciliation

Rule ID: VR-004-002 Rule Name: Cross-System Policy Existence (PolicyCenter ⟷ BillingCenter) Category: Referential Integrity Priority Level: HIGH SOP Reference: SOP 3.3 Description: Validates every PolicyCenter policy has corresponding BillingCenter record. Ensures billing system keeps pace with underwriting changes.

SOURCE TABLE(S):

pc_policyperiod (PolicyCenter)
bc_policy (BillingCenter)
TARGET RECORD(S):

All policies
Estimated volume (sample): 5,000 records
BUSINESS RULE: For every active or recently terminated policy in PolicyCenter: A corresponding record MUST exist in BillingCenter (Delayed sync acceptable if < 4 hour lag)

TECHNICAL IMPLEMENTATION: IF PolicyNumber IN (SELECT PolicyNumber FROM pc_policyperiod) AND PolicyNumber NOT IN (SELECT PolicyNumber FROM bc_policy) AND CreationTime < (NOW - 4 HOURS) THEN VIOLATION = TRUE (Missing BillingCenter record)

VALIDATION QUERY:

SELECT 'VR-004-002' as Rule_ID, pc.PolicyNumber, pc.Status as PC_Status, bc.PolicyNumber as BC_PolicyNumber, 'Missing BillingCenter Record' as Violation_Type, TIMESTAMP_DIFF(CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(), pc.CreationTime, HOUR) as Age_Hours FROM driiiportfolio.raw_underwriting_data.pc_policyperiod pc LEFT JOIN driiiportfolio.raw_underwriting_data.bc_policy bc ON pc.PolicyNumber = bc.PolicyNumber WHERE bc.PolicyNumber IS NULL AND TIMESTAMP_DIFF(CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(), pc.CreationTime, HOUR) > 4;

ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA:

Threshold: 0% (assuming < 4 hour lag tolerance)
Pass Condition: COUNT(violations_older_than_4hrs) = 0
Current Status: PASSING (0 violations > 4 hour lag)
EXCEPTION HANDLING:

New policies: Allow 4-hour lag for nightly batch integration
Cancelled policies: Allow 24-hour lag for billing adjustments
SEVERITY CLASSIFICATION:

Impact: HIGH (billing cannot process without PolicyCenter link)
Business Impact: Invoicing delays; commission processing failures
DETECTION TIMESTAMP:

Execution: Nightly batch (after BillingCenter load at 11 PM)
Latency Tolerance: <= 4 hours
REMEDIATION PATH:

