## Rule Execution Scheduling

### Execution Timeline

REAL-TIME (Triggered immediately on source change): ├─ VR-001-001: HB 2067 Reason Code (via Informatica CDI) ├─ VR-001-002: Agent ID (PolicyCenter validation endpoint) ├─ VR-002-001: Premium Positivity (PolicyCenter rating engine) ├─ VR-002-002: Date Logic (PolicyCenter validation) └─ VR-004-002: Cross-System Sync (via ETL trigger)

NIGHTLY BATCH (11:00 PM – 1:00 AM): ├─ SQL_01: HB 2067 Compliance Check (comprehensive) ├─ SQL_02: Referential Integrity Check ├─ SQL_03: Data Standards VIN Check ├─ SQL_04: Geocoding Completeness Check ├─ VR-004-001: Orphan Detection └─ Alert Generation & Escalation

WEEKLY GOVERNANCE REVIEW (Monday 9:00 AM): ├─ Violation trend analysis ├─ Rule effectiveness assessment ├─ Remediation plan review └─ Exception approvals

Code

---

## Exception & Override Procedures

### Exception Request Workflow

DETECTION ├─ Rule violation flagged ├─ Severity assessed └─ Issue logged to AIL

INVESTIGATION ├─ Data Quality Analyst investigates context ├─ Determines if legitimate exception or true violation └─ Documents findings

EXCEPTION REQUEST (if applicable) ├─ Submit to Data Governance Committee with: │ ├─ Rule ID and violation details │ ├─ Business justification for exception │ ├─ Proposed resolution/timeline │ └─ Risk assessment (if bypassing control) └─ Target approval: 48 hours

APPROVAL ├─ Data Governance Committee votes ├─ Exception recorded in Exception_Log table ├─ Rule may be temporarily disabled for affected records └─ Notification sent to stakeholders

REMEDIATION ├─ Implement fix per approved timeline ├─ Re-validate affected records ├─ Close exception request └─ Trend analysis for process improvement

Code

### Exception Categories

| Category | Examples | Approval Level | Typical Duration |
|----------|----------|-----------------|-------------------|
| **Data Quality Gap** | Historical data; legacy system; integration lag | Data Governance | 5–30 days |
| **System Configuration** | Validation endpoint not deployed; rule logic bug | IT + Governance | 1–7 days |
| **Business Process** | Legitimate multi-step workflow; delay acceptable | Business Owner | 30–90 days |
| **Regulatory Phase-In** | Gradual HB 2067 compliance rollout | Compliance Officer | 30–180 days |

---

## Rule Performance Metrics

### Query Performance Baseline (Sample: 5,000 records)

| Rule | Execution Time | Indexed | Memory Usage | Notes |
|------|----------------|---------|--------------|-------|
| VR-001-001 | 2.3s | Yes | 45 MB | LEFT JOIN adds overhead |
| VR-001-002 | 1.8s | Yes | 38 MB | Agent_Master lookup |
| VR-002-001 | 1.2s | Yes | 25 MB | Simple range check |
| VR-002-002 | 1.1s | Yes | 22 MB | Date arithmetic |
| VR-002-003 | 2.1s | Yes | 50 MB | Reference lookup |
| VR-003-001 | 1.9s | Yes | 40 MB | REGEXP_CONTAINS adds cost |
| VR-004-001 | 2.7s | Yes | 60 MB | Largest result set |
| VR-004-002 | 3.2s | Yes | 70 MB | Two large table joins |
| VR-005-001 | 1.5s | Yes | 35 MB | County filter efficient |

**Total Execution Time (All Rules Sequentially): ~17.8 seconds**  
**Recommended Batch Window: 30 minutes (to accommodate retries & escalation)**

