| VR-004-002 | 0 | 0 | 0 | N/A | N/A |
| VR-005-001 | 594 | 0 | 0 | 100% | 100% |

**Average Precision: 100% (no false positives detected)**

---

## Maintenance & Version Control

### Rule Change Management

**Change Request Process:**

INITIATE CHANGE ├─ Document business driver (regulatory, operational, technical) ├─ Assess impact on dependent systems/processes └─ Submit Change Request (CR) to Data Governance Committee

REVIEW & APPROVAL ├─ Technical review: Can rule logic be implemented in current platform? ├─ Business review: Does rule align with organizational policy? ├─ Risk review: What is impact if rule fails or is bypassed? └─ Approval requires consensus (target: 48–72 hours)

DEVELOPMENT & TESTING ├─ Update rule definition & SQL/CDQ logic ├─ Test in development environment (10% sample) ├─ Test in staging environment (full dataset) ├─ Document test results & edge cases └─ Peer code review (2 reviewers minimum)

DEPLOYMENT ├─ Schedule deployment during maintenance window ├─ Apply to production environment ├─ Monitor for elevated violations in first 24 hours ├─ Escalate if failure rate > expected └─ Document deployment details & rollback procedure

POST-DEPLOYMENT MONITORING ├─ Track violation trend for 2 weeks ├─ Tune thresholds if necessary ├─ Document lessons learned └─ Close Change Request

Version Control: ├─ All rule definitions stored in version control (Git) ├─ SQL queries tagged by version (v1.0, v1.1, etc.) ├─ Change log maintained: Who changed | When | Why └─ Rollback plan documented for each change

Code

### Version History (Sample)

| Rule ID | Version | Date | Change | Approver |
|---------|---------|------|--------|----------|
| VR-001-001 | 1.0 | 2026-04-01 | Initial HB 2067 compliance rule | Compliance |
| VR-001-001 | 1.1 | 2026-04-15 | Added UNION for missing vs. unmapped codes | DQ Analyst |
| VR-002-003 | 1.0 | 2026-04-01 | TDI reference table lookup | Underwriting |
| VR-003-001 | 1.0 | 2026-03-15 | Initial VIN format validation | Underwriting |
| VR-005-001 | 1.0 | 2026-04-10 | Coastal geocoding check | Catastrophe Mgmt |

### Quarterly Rule Assessment

**Schedule: Every 3 months (next: July 2026)**

Evaluation Criteria:
- Violation rate trend (increasing? decreasing? stable?)
- False positive rate (any new false alarms?)
- Rule effectiveness (catching real issues?)
- Threshold appropriateness (current thresholds still relevant?)
- Performance impact (query execution time acceptable?)
- Remediation effectiveness (are violations being fixed?)

**Outputs:**
- Quarterly Rule Performance Report
- Threshold adjustment recommendations
- New rules needed
- Rules to be retired or merged

