# Complete Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs)
## Operational Execution Framework for Data Quality Lifecycle

**Document Owner:** Data Governance Committee  
**Author:** Daniel Rodriguez III, Data Quality Analyst II  
**Date:** April 18, 2026  
Summary
This comprehensive Complete SOP Documentation provides:

✅ 8 fully detailed Standard Operating Procedures with step-by-step execution guidance for all operational activities

✅ SOP 1: End-to-End Data Quality Lifecycle Management – 7-step process (Ingestion → Profiling → Validation → Detection → RCA → Remediation → Closure)

✅ SOP 2: Data Profiling and Statistical Assessment – Daily dashboards, weekly deep-dives, quarterly reviews

✅ SOP 3: Validation Rule Execution – Real-time triggers, nightly batch scheduling, threshold evaluation, error handling

✅ SOP 4: Root Cause Analysis and Remediation – SMART problem definition, 5-Whys analysis, Fishbone diagrams, corrective action plans, post-mortem documentation

✅ SOP 5: Data Issue Management and Severity Escalation – CRITICAL/HIGH/MEDIUM/WARNING classifications with specific escalation paths and SLA tracking

✅ SOP 6: Data Quality KPI Monitoring and Reporting – 6-dimension framework (Accuracy, Completeness, Consistency, Timeliness, Validity, Integrity), daily/weekly/monthly reporting cadence

✅ SOP 7: Data Governance Execution and Data Dictionary Maintenance – Field metadata capture, naming standards, GDPR/DORA RoPA compliance

✅ SOP 8: SDLC Support and Release Readiness – Pre-release assessment, test case development, staging validation, production monitoring

✅ Appendices: Job schedules, contact directory, decision trees, templates, exception request forms

✅ Practical examples showing how to execute each step (actual SQL, email templates, dashboard metrics, escalation workflows)

This document transforms abstract governance principles into concrete, executable procedures that any team member can follow to maintain data quality excellence.

